Subject: [PATCH 05/13] rdna-boosts: block 05: flash-attention band, native
 quantized K/V and derived kq mask
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Band (RDNA4 WMMA GQA fold, wide verify band, GQA cap #133, the
ggml_set_fa_tensor_parallel hint), native quantized q8_0/q4_0/q4_1/q5_0/q5_1/
iq4_nl/bf16 K/V reads, the V3 derived kq-mask inputs (cell_pos/tok_lo/tok_hi),
the iq4_nl FA quants and the per-type tile instances.

The per-context fattn_stage prefill arena (and its RDNA3_5 prefill band split)
is deferred to block 10 slab-moe: here a native-capable operand is read natively
at every width and the F16 staging copy for a non-native type goes to the node's
reserved scratch (the pre-arena behaviour).

Env-read hygiene (no behaviour change): resolve GGML_CUDA_FA_WMMA_256 / GGML_CUDA_FA_WMMA_MAX_HEAD
once into values rather than caching the getenv() pointer (unsafe on Windows).

RDNA2 (gfx1030) FA gate fixes, reported and validated by @slavap (PR #181;
Radeon Pro V620 + RX 7900 XTX, ROCm 7.2.4, one gfx1030;gfx1100 build, the full
FLASH_ATTN_EXT and MUL_MAT backend-ops gates green on both cards).  Without them
the gfx1030 FLASH_ATTN_EXT gate aborted with "ROCm error: an illegal memory
access" and MUL_MAT was blocked behind it.  Three separate defects:

- ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_get_alloc_size (TILE branch): FATTN_KV_NATIVE_BF16
  is the *F16 staging* type on hardware without native BF16 tensor cores -- the
  tile case chooser only picks the BF16 instantiation under
  bf16_mma_hardware_available, and gfx1030 has no V_DOT2_F32_BF16 -- so mapping
  it to GGML_TYPE_BF16 left need_f16 false and let the whole-cache converter
  write past the node's allocation (sentinel clobber, then illegal access).
  The mapping now matches the chooser.  The same latent mismatch existed on
  RDNA1 and on pre-Ampere NVIDIA / older MUSA.
- launch_fattn_tile_switch_ncols1: the decode/verify band (Q->ne[1] <= 8) was
  the only one of the seven launch sites that omitted the q_h2 argument, so it
  defaulted to false while a wide RDNA2 kernel (q_global: GGML_CUDA_FATTN_TILE_
  Q_GLOBAL, DKQ <= 256, ncols >= 16) read Q from the Q_h2 global half2 buffer
  that was never allocated -- a null pointer and a fault near 0x1000 for GQA-16
  decode shapes (hsk=192, nr23=[16,1], n_q <= 8).  It now passes the same
  condition as the other six.
- ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_get_f16_extra_data: the ncols2 > 1 tile branch loads
  its KV tiles without out-of-bounds checks, so the last tile reads up to
  nbatch_fa - 1 rows past the operand.  The KV cache allocation has always had
  that slack, but the converted F16 scratch is exact size and sits at the end of
  the node's allocation, so it read into the next allocation.  A 511-row guard
  tail is now reserved after each converted operand (the nbatch_fa config field
  is 9 bits and the table asserts <= 256, so half is margin), gated on
  GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_RDNA2 so every other backend keeps its allocation sizes.

Fold (r92): the 2-byte band arm joins the 32-column band block, and the RDNA4
head-512 row goes back to upstream's shape.  (a) `ggml_cuda_fattn_band_wmma_ncols1()`
no longer special-cases f16/bf16 (native BF16) to 2 columns, and the 2-byte band split
drops from 3*nsm/4 to nsm/2.  The 2-column tile was the right default only while that arm
still selected the pre-band 128-half2 config row: with the band's own 64-half2 row it wins
~5 % at n_q = 1 and loses everywhere else, because ceil(n_q/2) output tiles each stream the
whole KV cache (head 256 GQA 6, gfx1201, us per call, f16 KV: n_q 1 760 -> 684, n_q 4
763 -> 695, n_q 8 1142 -> 823 at kv 98304; bf16 813/869/1451 -> 685/696/832).  The choice
stays width-independent, so W = 1..8 still reduce identically (GREEDY-PURITY.md §36).
(b) The `(512, 512, 32)` RDNA row -- the only head-512 row the AMD dispatcher can reach,
since `switch_ncols1` forces ncols = 32/ncols2 for DKQ > 256 -- was replaced by the
2026-09-14 RDNA prefill sweep with an 8-warp / 128-KV-row / nbatch_V2 16 config that is
~1.35x slower than the tile kernel, which made RDNA4's WMMA head cap of 576 a prefill
regression for every Gemma 4 global layer (issue #188).  Retuned to 4 warps, 32 KV rows,
one 128-half2 K/V batch, combine 64, Q in registers: gemma-4 31B global-attn shape (D=512,
4 KV heads, 32 Q heads, ub 512, q8_0 KV) 32768 126.1 -> 42.3 ms and 98304 377.0 -> 128.1 ms,
end to end pp512 +95 % at d32768 and +144 % at d98304 (31B and 26B-A4B).  Records:
archive/work/fa-band-2byte-row/, upstream/UPSTREAM-PR-fa-512-rdna-head-cap/.

Fold (r98, PR #195, @overdoingism): with q8_0 K and V read in place (decode/verify, up to 8 query rows)
the RDNA4 band launches a second kernel variant, `flash_attn_ext_f16<..., band_fetch_ahead = true>`, which
fetches the raw q8_0 bytes of the next K/V batches into registers ahead of use and converts a batch into
shared memory only when it is due; its barriers order shared memory only (release / s_barrier / acquire on
"local"), because `__syncthreads()` also waits for every outstanding global load and would drain the fetches
at the next barrier.  The quants stay packed in 32-bit words, with an empty `asm volatile` pinning the
conversion at the stage point (otherwise the compiler unpacks the bytes right after the fetch, which waits
there and needs 4x the registers).  64-column block (widths 5..8): two batches in flight, Q in registers.
32-column block (widths 1..4): one batch in flight and the stream continues across the iteration boundary
into the next KV block that is not fully masked, Q read from shared memory (a register-resident Q is spilled
there and its scratch reloads share the load counter with the fetched K/V).  The variant is compiled in two
generated translation units of its own (`template-instances/fattn-mma-f16-band-fetch-ahead-ncols1_{4,8}-
ncols2_8-dkq256-dv256.cu`, emitted by generate_cu_files.py), so every other launch, including f16 / bf16 K/V
and prefill, compiles to the same gfx1201 instructions as before it (verified at the assembly level: 0
differing instructions in both dkq256 band instances, a dkq128 instance, the tile and vec units and
fattn.cu).  Default on; `GGML_HIP_FA_BAND_FETCH_AHEAD=0` runs the kernel without it for q8_0 too.  It also
keys the FA shared-memory attribute raise per (variant, device) rather than per device, so the two kernels
cannot share one "already raised" flag.

Gates (gfx1201, ROCm 10.1.0, 27B UD-Q4_K_XL with q8_0 K/V unless noted): bit-identical to r97 everywhere
the variant fires -- `test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT` 6391/6391 on both builds, prefill-logit KLD
0.000000 / same-top-p 100.000 %, greedy text identical at 8K and 110K context, on a 2 GPU tensor split and
on gemma4 12B (its head-256 SWA layers), the 4-axis adaptive MTP gate at -n 3000 (text and draft acceptance
identical on all four axes) and n7 = plain; `llama-batched-bench -npp 16 -ntg 32 -npl 1,4,8` B=1 29.47 ->
30.12 t/s, B=4 95.73 -> 97.70, B=8 flat; decode +0.7 % at 8K and +2.4 % at 110K context (3 interleaved pairs
each; prefill unchanged at 840 t/s), +0.9 % on the 2 GPU tensor split.

Fold (r99, PR #198, @slavap): two RDNA2 (gfx1030) FA follow-ups from the review of PR #181, plus the
arch-independent half they needed.

- **One tile K/V type selection.**  The tile kernel has a single K/V type parameter and its choice was kept
  by hand in two places: the instantiation (`ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_tile_case_type`, `fattn-tile.cu`) and
  the F16 scratch sizing (`ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_get_alloc_size`, `fattn.cu`).  They had drifted three
  times (the missing q4_0 arm, the mixed-K/V NaNs, the missing RDNA2 bf16 scratch).  Both now call one
  `ggml_cuda_fattn_tile_type(K, V, cc)` in `fattn-rdna.cuh`: BF16 only where the hardware reads it natively,
  else the native dequant type, else F16 (BF16 without native support maps to F16, i.e. the launcher
  converts).  The mapping is 1:1 with the previous order on every arch, the instantiation set is unchanged
  (96 tile objects before and after) and the host change leaves every tile kernel's gfx1201 ISA identical.
- **Checked tail for the last unchecked tile (RDNA2 only).**  The `ncols2 > 1` tile branch loads its KV
  tiles without out-of-bounds checks, so its last tile can read up to `nbatch_fa - 1` rows past the KV data.
  In a model that stays inside the KV cache tensor's slack, but an exact-size operand (test-backend-ops) can
  reach the neighbouring allocation.  On RDNA2 the last tile now takes the already-compiled
  `oob_check = true` form (zero-fills the tail and keeps it out of the softmax).  Every other target is
  untouched: `RDNA2` is defined only in the gfx103x device pass (`vendors/hip.h`), the added block is inside
  `#if defined(RDNA2)`, and the gfx1201 tile instances are byte-identical in ISA to r98.
- **The 511-row guard tail is kept** and its derivation documented: `nbatch_fa` is a 9-bit config field but
  `GGML_CUDA_FATTN_TILE_CONFIG_CASE` static_asserts `<= 256`, each K chunk loads `nbatch_fa` rows and each V
  chunk `nbatch_V` with `static_assert(nbatch_fa % nbatch_V == 0)`, so the over-read is at most `255` rows;
  511 = 2 x 256 - 1.  Since the RDNA2 tail is now checked, the tail is belt-and-braces, not the only
  protection.  Comment only: no allocation size changes on any backend.

Gates (gfx1201, ROCm 10.1.0): `test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT` 6391/6391 (identical per case to r98),
prefill-logit KLD 0.000000 / 100.000 %, greedy text identical to r98, `validate-set.sh` green, per-block
build green.  A `gfx1201;gfx1030` dual-target build compiles the RDNA2 arm; the RDNA2 runtime gate is the
reporter's (Radeon Pro V620, ROCm 7.2.4: FLASH_ATTN_EXT 6389/6389, MUL_MAT 2444/2444 with the add-on, and
the same on gfx1100).

RDNA3_0 (gfx1100) head-512 WMMA prefill rows, reported by @briansp2020 (PR #199;
RX 7900 XTX).  The RDNA head-512 rows were tuned on gfx1201 and keep Q in
registers, so on gfx1100 every head-512 kernel sat at the 256-VGPR limit and
spilled (~1.0-1.4k VGPRs per lane); head 512 was therefore capped back to the
tile kernel on RDNA3_0 in r5 (issue #30).  RDNA3_0 now has its own rows for
DKQ == DV == 512 (Q in shared memory, 128 threads, 64-wide K/V/combine
batches), and head 512 takes WMMA prefill again on top of the 256 cap: other
heads above 256 keep the tile kernel, RDNA4/RDNA3_5 rows are unchanged and the
decode/verify band stays on the tile kernel.  GGML_CUDA_FA_RDNA3_WMMA_512=0
disables it; GGML_CUDA_FA_WMMA_256=0 and GGML_CUDA_FA_WMMA_MAX_HEAD still take
it out (the rows are RDNA3_0-only, so MAX_HEAD only decides whether head 512
takes WMMA at all).

Measured on gfx1100 (gemma-4-26B-A4B QAT UD-Q4_K_XL, q8_0 KV, pp2048):
d32768 1908.3/1909.2 -> 2549.1/2554.6 t/s (+34 %), d65536 1209.3/1207.6 ->
1756.2/1757.5 (+45 %), tg128 at d32768 unchanged (127.74/127.74 ->
127.80/127.73).  FLASH_ATTN_EXT 6391/6391 on gfx1100; the switch-off text is
bit-identical to r101 and gfx1201/gfx1151 output is unchanged (byte-identical on
gemma4-26B-A4B).

Prefill-logit NOTE (known limitation, TODO #81 / wip/fa-rdna3-head512-purity):
this is a tile->WMMA family switch, so it moves the prefill logits against the
tile kernel: mean KLD 0.0293 / same-top-p 92.59 % on that model at the gate's
out-of-domain point (PPL 604), i.e. it does NOT meet the absolute 0.005 / 98 %
gate.  Calibrated at the same point: the head-256 WMMA rows the delivery has
shipped default-on for gfx1100 since r5 measure 0.0441 / 90.63 %, a benign
ubatch change on the same kernel ~0.12 per chunk, and the issue-#113 BF16
chunked GDN 0.62.  PPL is unchanged within its +/-5 % error bar (f16 KV 604.06
vs 607.20, q8_0 KV 617.85 vs 620.59).  Accepted as no worse than the shipped
equivalent switch; the campaign above exists to close the gap.

Hybrid and DSA kq-mask fill sites carry the guard the rest of the file has (reported,
root-caused and validated by @RikshaDriver; RX 7600 gfx1102, ROCm 10.1, bailingmoe3 /
Ling-3.0-tiny-IQ4_NL, delivery v14-3f03b1772-r128).  A single-sequence context aborted
before the first token: GGML_ASSERT(buffer) at ggml-backend.cpp:571, via
ggml_backend_buffer_is_host <- llama_kv_cache::set_input_kq_mask <-
llm_graph_input_mem_hybrid_k::set_input <- llm_graph_result::set_inputs.  The derived
form leaves the packed mask with no consumer and the allocator gives unconsumed tensors
no buffer; ten of the thirteen fill sites in this file already guard for exactly that
(llm_graph_input_attn_kv is the origin, see upstream/attn-k-null-mask-guard), and three
did not: llm_graph_input_attn_k_dsa (its mla and lid masks) and llm_graph_input_mem_hybrid_k.
The hybrid class is the one a bailingmoe3 graph reaches - 18 KDA + 6 MLA layers, and only a
single-sequence context enables the derived form (`multi_stream = n_seqs > 1 &&
(!kv_unified || arch == DEEPSEEK4)`), which is why -np 2 and above never reach it.
llm_graph_input_mem_hybrid::set_input guards the identical call, so the hybrid-K class was
the odd one out.  Measured on the RX 7600 with -st -n 128, card idle, 2 reps: -np 1
GGML_ASSERT(buffer) rc 134 -> 88.5 / 87.0 t/s; -np 2 87.1 / 88.2 and -np 4 87.4 / 88.0
unchanged, the derived form being off at 2+ slots in both builds.  Ruled out by building:
the recurrent state (n_rs = 1, ne0 = 1 at the assert), ggml_set_output(inp->s_copy) with
the line deleted (still aborts), ctx size 4096 / 32768 / 131072, flash-attn on/off, -ngl
0..999, the quant.  can_reuse needs nothing: can_reuse_kq_mask() reads only ne[], not
buffer.  Work-around without this: LLAMA_KQ_MASK_DERIVED=0 (measured free at this shape,
88.5 / 88.8).
